From 74d8aa23a86deecf215a9050e23c83ceb3f28ab4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 22:18:22 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 149/152] dns: the AAAA question of a name without an IPv4
 address goes out under ipv4_only

The strategy ipv4_only answers every AAAA question with no address, so a
name that has only IPv6 addresses does not resolve. With dns.ipv6_if_no_ipv4
an AAAA question goes out when the A question of its name, through the same
server, is answered without an A record; a lookup of such a name takes its
IPv6 addresses. A name with an IPv4 address keeps the empty answer, and a
FakeIP server is not asked. The A question goes through the cache, which a
client asking A and AAAA together shares.
---
